"""
Chroma Diagnostic Tool v4.1
=================================

Fixes in 4.1.1
--------------
- Script parses again (placeholder INPUT_DIR/OUTPUT_DIR were invalid syntax).
- RGB->XYZ no longer scales by the white point twice; neutral grey now has
  C*ab = 0 (it previously read ~6-10).
- Pixels converted by an ICC transform are no longer re-decoded with the
  source space's gamma/primaries.  Standard profiles (sRGB / Adobe RGB /
  ProPhoto) are decoded analytically at full precision instead.
- ICC profile names and EXIF ColorSpace are actually read now (bytes were
  passed to ImageCmsProfile; EXIF was read after exif_transpose dropped it).
- Untagged images default to sRGB (--default-colorspace to override).
- 16-bit RGB TIFF/PNG are read at 16 bits; 16-bit greyscale no longer
  saturates to white.
- Segmented-map background is dark greyscale instead of solid black.
- New default threshold mode "noise_floor" (substrate histogram peak +
  noise cutoff, as described in the README); percentile/otsu/fixed remain.
- Sensitivity masks use the same clamp and spatial filter as the output mask.
- output_dir inside input_dir is not re-ingested; montage text no longer
  clipped; u16 sidecar scaling recorded and guarded against divide-by-zero.

Refactored batch chroma analysis with corrected LRC interpolation,
bit-depth preservation, vectorized spatial filtering, and FADGI-compliant
color-space management.

Key fixes from v4.0
---------------------
1. Color-space awareness: detects EXIF ColorSpace tag and ICC profile name;
   defaulted to ProPhoto RGB when no space was declared (sRGB since 4.1.1).
   Custom RGB->XYZ->LAB pipeline replaces OpenCV's
   hard-coded sRGB assumption.
2. Critical bug fixes:
   - FOOTER_HEIGHT / MONTAGE_FOOTER_HEIGHT now defined.
   - process_image() indentation corrected (was nested inside _process_single_space).
   - _create_segmented_visual() "cls" typo fixed.
   - _compute_lrc() double-convolution bug fixed.
   - _open_working_rgb() max_val logic corrected after ICC transform.
   - Categorical mask saved as 16-bit raw rather than 8-bit "L" mode.
3. Bradford chromatic adaptation for ProPhoto RGB (D50 -> D65) before LAB.
4. Gamma curves: sRGB (piecewise), Adobe RGB (gamma 2.2), ProPhoto (gamma 1.8).
"""

